WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.575
Aladdin started walking toward home.

2
00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:12.289
After a while, the desert ended, and Aladdin was again in a cool, green garden.

3
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.413
He saw the place where he and Magrib had rested under the tree.

4
00:00:17.414 --> 00:00:19.574
"That man!" he thought.

5
00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:22.722
"I hope I never see him again!"

6
00:00:22.723 --> 00:00:27.155
When Aladdin saw the city gate, he walked faster.

7
00:00:27.156 --> 00:00:32.456
Soon he was through the bazaar and walking down the street of crooked houses.

8
00:00:32.457 --> 00:00:37.258
He ran to his house, pushed the door open, and stepped inside.

9
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:42.134
Aladdin’s mother dropped her spinning and raised her hands in the air.

10
00:00:42.135 --> 00:00:47.875
"Praise be to God!" she cried. "You’re alive!"

11
00:00:47.876 --> 00:00:52.630
"Mother," Aladdin said and immediately fainted.

12
00:00:52.631 --> 00:00:59.839
"My son!" Zeba grabbed a cup of water and went to her son, who had fallen on the floor.

13
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.611
She gently poured the water over Aladdin’s head.

14
00:01:04.612 --> 00:01:08.355
"Oh," he cried as he awoke.

15
00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:12.038
"I have been sick with worry," she said.

16
00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:17.514
"Where have you been all day and night?"

17
00:01:17.515 --> 00:01:18.908
"I will tell you,"

18
00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:22.921
answered Aladdin, wiping water from his eyes.

19
00:01:22.922 --> 00:01:25.136
"I was led far from home.

20
00:01:25.137 --> 00:01:30.275
I was sent underground, locked up, and then left to die.

21
00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:32.523
I was cold and hungry.

22
00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:35.724
And now I am being drowned!"

23
00:01:35.725 --> 00:01:39.709
Zeba’s eyes opened wide and she dropped her cup.

24
00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.080
"What happened? Where is your uncle?"

25
00:01:43.081 --> 00:01:46.320
"He is not my uncle," cried Aladdin.

26
00:01:46.321 --> 00:01:48.725
"He is a liar and an evil magician.

27
00:01:48.726 --> 00:01:51.343
I’m amazed that I am still alive!"

28
00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:54.721
"But your uncle said―"

29
00:01:54.722 --> 00:01:56.396
"He is not my uncle!

30
00:01:56.397 --> 00:01:58.853
His kindness was false!

31
00:01:58.854 --> 00:02:00.619
His promises were tricks.

32
00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.653
He planned to kill me all along!"

33
00:02:03.654 --> 00:02:09.923
Zeba turned pale, and Aladdin put his arms around her.

34
00:02:09.924 --> 00:02:17.109
Then he told her everything about the long walk, the enchanted treasury, and the lamp.

35
00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:22.201
He showed her the glass fruit and the lamp.

36
00:02:22.202 --> 00:02:27.697
"Because of the glass fruit," he explained, "I could not hand the lamp to Magrib.

37
00:02:27.698 --> 00:02:33.271
Then, in his anger, he buried me alive in the treasury and left."

38
00:02:33.272 --> 00:02:36.286
Aladdin sank onto a cushion.

39
00:02:36.287 --> 00:02:43.612
"I have eaten only a cookie and a fig since yesterday."

40
00:02:43.613 --> 00:02:47.023
"Take this, Aladdin," said his mother.

41
00:02:47.024 --> 00:02:51.297
She gave her son the last piece of bread in the house.

42
00:02:51.298 --> 00:02:57.589
When he had finished eating, he went to sleep right where he sat.

43
00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.689
Aladdin didn’t awaken until noon the next day.

44
00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:05.843
He sat up and stretched his arms over his head.

45
00:03:05.844 --> 00:03:08.422
"I am hungry, Mother," he said.

46
00:03:08.423 --> 00:03:11.461
"May I have something to eat?"

47
00:03:11.462 --> 00:03:15.028
Zeba shook her head as she spun her wool.

48
00:03:15.029 --> 00:03:19.796
"There is no more food in the house, my son, and no money.

49
00:03:19.797 --> 00:03:23.366
But see, I have spun a little bit of yarn.

50
00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:26.704
I will take it to the market and sell it.

51
00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:29.763
Then I will buy some bread."

52
00:03:29.764 --> 00:03:30.932
"Keep your yarn,"

53
00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:34.289
Aladdin replied, rising from his cushion.

54
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.916
"I will take the brass lamp to the market and sell that."

55
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:42.133
He started to put the lamp back into his pocket.

56
00:03:42.134 --> 00:03:45.179
"Wait, son," said Zeba.

57
00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.103
"The lamp is very dirty.

58
00:03:47.104 --> 00:03:51.350
If I polish it, it will bring a higher price."

59
00:03:51.351 --> 00:03:54.897
She took a cloth and began rubbing the lamp.

60
00:03:54.898 --> 00:04:01.188
In the next moment, smoke swirled overhead and music filled the room.

61
00:04:01.189 --> 00:04:06.706
"What is happening?" screamed Zeba. "Help!"

62
00:04:06.707 --> 00:04:12.510
"Your wish is my command," boomed a voice in the smoke.

63
00:04:12.511 --> 00:04:15.918
The music stopped and the smoke cleared.

64
00:04:15.919 --> 00:04:21.945
Another genie stood before them!

